  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\tan ^{-1}\\left[\\frac{1}{1+1.2}\\right]+\\tan ^{-1}\\left[\\frac{1}{1+2.3}\\right]+$ $\\ldots+\\tan ^{-1}\\left[\\frac{1}{1+n(n+1)}\\right]=\\tan ^{-1}[x]$, then $x$ is\nequal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{n+1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{n}{n+1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{n+2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{n}{n+2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { Given } \\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{1+1.2}\\right)+\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{1+2.3}\\right)+\\ldots \\\\ & +\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{1+n(n+1)}\\right)=\\tan ^{-1}(x)\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} \\Rightarrow \\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2-1}{1+1.2}\\right) & +\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3-2}{1+2.3}\\right)+\\ldots \\\\ & +\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{n+1-n}{1+n(n+1)}\\right)=\\tan ^{-1}(x)\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow \\tan ^{-1}(2)-\\tan ^{-1}(1)+\\tan ^{-1}(3)-\\tan ^{-1}(2)+\\ldots \\\\ & +\\tan ^{-1}(\\mathrm{n}+1)-\\tan ^{-1}(\\mathrm{n})=\\tan ^{-1}(x)\\end{aligned}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\tan ^{-1}(\\mathrm{n}+1)-\\tan ^{-1}(1)=\\tan ^{-1}(x)$\n$\\left\\{\\because \\tan ^{-1}(A)-\\tan ^{-1}(B)=\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{A-B}{1+A \\cdot B}\\right)\\right\\}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{n}{n+2}\\right)=\\tan ^{-1}(x) \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{n}{n+2}$"
  }
